  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4e54ef0d220210343bd1afb93b700b74, type: 3}
  m_Name: Bakery_Memory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: TidyUp.Runtime::TidyUp.Story.MemoryDefinition
  _id: memory_bakery
  _title: The Day Before
  _locationName: The Bakery, Old Town Market
  _lines:
  - Speaker: 
    Text: Five o'clock in the morning. The ovens hum, and the whole street smells of crust and butter.
    Duration: 5
  - Speaker: Hugo the baker
    Text: Baguettes on top, loaves in the middle, croissants low, where the little ones can reach. Same as every morning.
    Duration: 6
  - Speaker: 
    Text: A soft knock at the back door. Nobody there. Only a trail of tiny footprints in the spilled flour, skipping out into the street.
    Duration: 6
  - Speaker: Hugo the baker
    Text: Odd. And last night the clock on the square struck thirteen. I counted twice.
    Duration: 5
  - Speaker: 
    Text: Hugo laughed, dusted off his apron, and set tomorrow's dough to rise.
    Duration: 4.5
  - Speaker: 
    Text: By morning, every loaf in the city had forgotten where it belonged.
    Duration: 5
  _clue: Tiny footprints in the flour, and the clock on the square striking thirteen, the night before the Muddle.
